  "question": {
    "text": "Water is being filled at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>sec</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in a right circular conical vessel (vertex downwards) of height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;and diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>. When the height of the water level is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>cm</mi></math>, the rate (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>) at which the wet conical surface area of the vessel increases is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gjrmy",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
